  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent-description; overall-intent-description: The scene depicts a window cleaner, wearing a blue shirt and cap, diligently wiping a window with a cloth, while the reflection of his actions is visible. The text overlay reads: 'when you wipe 700 times and there is still shit' (top), 'i have a question. for god.' (middle), and 'why?' (bottom). The overall intent is to humorously express exasperation or disbelief at a situation that defies logic or reason — specifically, the absurdity of persistently trying to fix something that remains unresolved or unfixable. The meme uses the visual of the cleaner's futile effort to symbolize a universal human experience of frustration when faced with persistent problems. There is no toxicity present in this meme. It does not target any specific group or individual based on protected characteristics, nor does it contain abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or propagandistic content. The intent is purely comedic and relatable, using the juxtaposition of the image (the cleaner’s effort) with the text (the rhetorical question) to create a humorous effect about the futility of certain endeavors.",
